"""chatter-gui src-tauri — Tauri v2 desktop validation app (Path A wrapper).

Bazel does not compile the Rust backend. `cargo tauri build` drives the full
multi-stage bundle (Vite SPA build → cargo rustc → platform bundler → code
signing / DMG / MSI / AppImage), which rules_rust doesn't model.

Boundary:
  - Bazel:  builds the intra-workspace Rust crates this app depends on
            (talkbank-model, talkbank-transform, send2clan-sys). Listed
            under `data` so any other Bazel consumer keeps building them
            and CI ordering stays sane.
  - Cargo:  resolves path-deps via Cargo.toml independently and runs
            `cargo tauri build` end-to-end against the live workspace
            (via `$BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` inside the wrapper script).

Known tradeoff: each of the three intra-workspace crates is compiled twice
(once by Bazel for downstream consumers, once by Cargo for the Tauri app).
The usual rlib-sharing workaround (`RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache`) is intentionally
not wired here — see `book/src/contributing/compile-times.md` for why
sccache is disabled in this workspace.

Dev (hot reload) is NOT wrapped — run `cargo tauri dev` from
`apps/chatter/chatter-gui/` directly when iterating.

Unit + integration tests on the Rust backend continue to run via `cargo
nextest run -p chatter-gui` (see top-level CLAUDE.md).
"""

load("@rules_shell//shell:sh_binary.bzl", "sh_binary")

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

sh_binary(
    name = "bundle",
    srcs = ["//bazel/chatter-tauri:bundle.sh"],
    data = [
        "//crates/clan/send2clan-sys:send2clan_sys",
        "//crates/core/talkbank-model:talkbank_model",
        "//crates/core/talkbank-transform:talkbank_transform",
        "//crates/core/talkbank-cache:talkbank_cache",
    ],
)
